{:edb/db-before-t 1655 :edb/db-after-t 1656 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534968 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:52:01.287Z" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186061614 1078 #edb/ref 17592186061617 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186064163 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446077 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186064163 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446078 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186064163 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446080 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186064164 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446075 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186064164 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446076 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186064164 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446079 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186064451 1050 840.0 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186064572 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186064572 1071 "Find  the global maximum value of the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ on the closed interval $\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le 2.$" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186064572 1071 "Find the global maximum value of the function $f(x) = \\frac{1}{x}$ on the closed interval $\\frac{1}{2} \\le x \\le 2$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139534968 17592186045417 false] [17592186064572 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe can see that ${f}^{′}(x)<0$ for all real values of $x.$ So there is no solution for ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ \n\nSo, the only critical points are the endpoints $x=\\frac{1}{2},2$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{2})}=2 \\\\ f(2) & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(\\frac{1}{2})=2,$ so the global maximum is $2.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(2)=\\frac{1}{2},$ so the global minimum is $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n![](images/ae/aef1d6e33213def71ada4a59f7d79b9f045083b2c501a752e81994e33f100277.png)" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186292684 1071 "For the function $f(x)={x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+9x+3,$ on the closed interval $-4\\le x\\le -2,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The global maximum value is $3$\n- The global minimum value is $1$\n- The global minimum value is $-1$" 13194139534968 17592186045417 false] [17592186292684 1071 "For the function $f(x)={x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+9x+3,$ on the closed interval $-4\\le x\\le -2,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The global maximum value is $3$\n\nII. The global minimum value is $1$\n\nIII. The global minimum value is $-1$" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446051 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446051 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446051 1083 #uuid "14e95874-53a9-59eb-a59d-1506787a86d4" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446052 1080 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446052 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446052 1083 #uuid "28e244bd-f5d9-59e7-bae1-37bf7dad0604" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446053 1080 "II only" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446053 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446053 1083 #uuid "2ac06203-f450-56e6-bf00-f392cec8e021" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446054 1080 "III only" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446054 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446054 1083 #uuid "52810d71-5114-5feb-ae18-a48ef7e104ee" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446055 1080 "II and III only" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446055 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13