-1" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446070 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446064 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446070 1079 #uuid "3d8e368b-ffbe-5e66-824e-4093e6579f11" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446071 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446067 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446071 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446071 1077 "field-1" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446071 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446067 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446071 1079 #uuid "6dd21141-a64a-59a6-830b-705be2c9af59" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446053 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446058 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446059 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446062 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446066 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446072 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446072 1077 "selection" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446072 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446066 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446072 1079 #uuid "b81fbc27-5dd0-5c38-b035-b8bc202627e0" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446051 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446052 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446057 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446063 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446065 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446073 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446073 1077 "selection" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446073 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446065 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446073 1079 #uuid "eafc929c-fdf4-5237-8e6e-4e3e669ade96" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446074 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446054 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446074 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446055 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446074 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446056 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446074 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446060 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446074 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446061 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446074 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446074 1077 "selection" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446074 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446055 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446074 1079 #uuid "ecc7805a-aaf8-5454-ad50-b7b1a50aac12" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446075 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446069 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446075 1069 "q-344474" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446075 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446075 1071 "The exact global maximum value of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ on the closed interval $0\\le x\\le 2\\pi $ is{{field-1}}." 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446075 1072 #uuid "264068ae-fe2b-5f78-b146-741b451e1198" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446075 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer. We discard all solutions except $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi =\\frac{5\\pi }{4},$ since they are the only values that belong to the given interval.\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{5\\pi }{4},$ and the endpoints $x=0,\\,2\\pi $ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1 \\\\ f\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ f\\,(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) & =sin\\,(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})+cos\\,(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ f(2\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\sqrt{2},$ so the global maximum is $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n- The least value is $f\\,(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})=-\\sqrt{2},$ so the global minimum is $-\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n![](images/e4/e42ca640ae08d60ea81bdcb7c3c3753f5dc74fb6eea49b5b0f999e3463b5f8f0.png)" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446076 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446070 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446076 1069 "q-344434" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446076 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446076 1071 "The exact global minimum value of the function $f(x)={x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2$ on the closed interval $-1\\le x\\le 1$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446076 1072 #uuid "4034162d-ab25-585a-b5bc-dfd3804a541e" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446076 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)={x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2}-6x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-6x & =0 \\\\ 3x(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ does not belong to the interval $[-1,1],$ the critical points are $x=0$ and the endpoints $x=-1,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =(-1)^{3}-3(-1)^{2}+2=-1-3+2=-2 \\\\ f(0) & =(0)^{3}-3(0)^{2}+2=2 \\\\ f(1) & =(1)^{3}-3(1)^{2}+2=1-3+2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(0)=2,$ so the global maximum is $2.$\n\n- The least value is $f(-1)=-2,$ so the global minimum is $-2.$\n\n![](images/39/3939bd8d9b8efd0be9381087b9b1802ee9bebd4fad620b855904f87d3bc61a86.png)" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446077 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446074 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446077 1069 "q-3012" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446077 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446077 1071 "For the function $f(x)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+3),$ defined on the closed interval $-2\\le x\\le 0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The global maximum value is $1$\n\nII. The global maximum value is $0$\n\nIII. The global minimum value is $-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)$" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446077 1072 #uuid "4194a834-6555-5df2-9764-fffba77d3eaf" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446077 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+3),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that ${f}^{′}(x)<0$ for all values of $x\\in [-2,0].$  So there is no solution for ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$\n\nSo, the only critical points are the endpoints $x=-2,0$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-2+3)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)=0 \\\\ f(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0+3)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)≈-1.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(-2)=0,$ so the global maximum is $0.$\n\n- The least value is $f(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3),$ so the global minimum is $-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"\n\n![](images/85/8578b190927c38e37fc5956d1b953539e41ea3e25f2e6ced48f21086722fdd43.png)" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446078 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446071 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446078 1069 "q-344386" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446078 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446078 1071 "The global minimum value of the function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{x+5}$ on the closed interval $0\\le x\\le 4$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446078 1072 #uuid "4f007c55-3624-5699-862a-6b2181c2b793" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446078 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{x}{x+5},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{5}{(x+5)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe can see that ${f}^{′}(x)>0$ for all real values of $x.$ So there is no solution for ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$\n\nSo, the only critical points are the endpoints $x=0,4$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\\frac{0}{(0+5)}=0 \\\\ f(4) & =\\frac{4}{(4+5)}=\\frac{4}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(4)=\\frac{4}{9},$ so the global maximum is $\\frac{4}{9}.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(0)=0,$ so the global minimum is $0.$\n\n![](images/73/731aff75eb5930d89e1306c44c34986ba2f92b5761971dcc9cbe3571963f2ab2.png)" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446079 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446073 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446079 1069 "q-3011" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446079 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446079 1071 "Find the global maximum value of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ on the closed interval $0\\le x\\le 2\\pi .$" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446079 1072 #uuid "6d6fccce-a1a6-5495-8484-833c6aab421e" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446079 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-1 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer. We discard all solutions except $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi =\\frac{7\\pi }{4},$ since they are the only values that belong to the given interval.\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{7\\pi }{4},$ and the endpoints $x=0,\\,2\\pi $ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=-1 \\\\ f(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ f(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})=-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ f(2\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=\\sqrt{2},$ so the global maximum is $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})=-\\sqrt{2},$ so the global minimum is $-\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n![](images/76/7645cecb4fef2af4f2e2061752957981414d63700de016ca4a535c8df219597e.png)" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446080 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446072 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446080 1069 "q-113771" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446080 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446080 1071 "For the function $f(x)=({x}^{2}+1){e}^{x},$ defined on the closed interval $[-2,0],$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The global minimum value is $\\frac{5}{{e}^{2}}$\n\nII. The global minimum value is $\\frac{2}{e}$\n\nIII. The global maximum value is $1$" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446080 1072 #uuid "b5c74e5b-a85a-561f-a53c-37938e4b9091" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true] [17592186446080 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=({x}^{2}+1){e}^{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =2x{e}^{x}+({x}^{2}+1){e}^{x} \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2x+1){e}^{x} \\\\  & =(x+1)^{2}{e}^{x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n(x+1)^{2}{e}^{x}=0\\,⟹\\,x=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=-1,$ and the endpoints $x=-2,0$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =((-2)^{2}+1){e}^{-2}=\\frac{5}{{e}^{2}}≈0.68 \\\\ f(-1) & =((-1)^{2}+1){e}^{-1}=\\frac{2}{e}≈0.74 \\\\ f(0) & =({0}^{2}+1){e}^{0}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(0)=1,$ so the global maximum is $1.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(-2)=\\frac{5}{{e}^{2}},$ so the global minimum is $\\frac{5}{{e}^{2}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"\n\n![](images/87/8768b85a24b4351a481fec2801be274990b2e524a7322bfcf07b257884b9409f.png)" 13194139534968 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-14e95874-53a9-59eb-a59d-1506787a86d4" 17592186446051 "answer-28e244bd-f5d9-59e7-bae1-37bf7dad0604" 17592186446052 "answer-2ac06203-f450-56e6-bf00-f392cec8e021" 17592186446053 "answer-52810d71-5114-5feb-ae18-a48ef7e104ee" 17592186446054 "answer-5e847e93-be00-5b15-bfac-543002b0dde8" 17592186446055 "answer-8141d386-0404-52e8-8de7-454bc213ddad" 17592186446056 "answer-83b3d4b4-9193-548b-92d2-89f90a26ba3f" 17592186446057 "answer-8cf8af1a-e65d-55f1-b5aa-0f6499f2e0f0" 17592186446058 "answer-9ddd95b3-37c0-5ea8-91de-762536f3b73e" 17592186446059 "answer-a1847c55-c1ef-5d11-9f47-66ad60e3ea46" 17592186446060 "answer-a675690c-021e-5075-9cda-7de9a1641938" 17592186446061 "answer-a6844010-1c33-526d-ac0d-05736327a1ba" 17592186446062 "answer-bf0fca65-f9f6-5b4c-986e-f335607b1999" 17592186446063 "answer-c57ecb3d-6b4a-5770-a83e-208ec453a7de" 17592186446064 "answer-cca7c6b4-7bda-5ecf-9402-b6c9fb9f1393" 17592186446065 "answer-dcc3be7e-6fd6-5b52-bdfd-43707a36bdc3" 17592186446066 "answer-f0070102-4be6-521a-a2c3-b7b69545cf7f" 17592186446067 "answer-f860dfb5-9cc2-564b-a719-e277d51c0fab" 17592186446068 "answer-field-0d0bc8af-0212-5f26-b710-65114290ccbb" 17592186446069 "answer-field-3d8e368b-ffbe-5e66-824e-4093e6579f11" 17592186446070 "answer-field-6dd21141-a64a-59a6-830b-705be2c9af59" 17592186446071 "answer-field-b81fbc27-5dd0-5c38-b035-b8bc202627e0" 17592186446072 "answer-field-eafc929c-fdf4-5237-8e6e-4e3e669ade96" 17592186446073 "answer-field-ecc7805a-aaf8-5454-ad50-b7b1a50aac12" 17592186446074 "question-264068ae-fe2b-5f78-b146-741b451e1198" 17592186446075 "question-4034162d-ab25-585a-b5bc-dfd3804a541e" 17592186446076 "question-4194a834-6555-5df2-9764-fffba77d3eaf" 17592186446077 "question-4f007c55-3624-5699-862a-6b2181c2b793" 17592186446078 "question-6d6fccce-a1a6-5495-84